; Forward again, seven cards a segment in (kind, s, wf, after, imm, nvs, pfw), four out (s, fs, pf, bef). A
; consonant's stress (Klatt 1979): 1 when a stressed vowel of its word comes right after it (imm), or when no vowel
; of its word comes before it (bef 0) and the word's next vowel is stressed (nvs); else 0. fs: the segment is in
; its word's last syllable, no vowel after it and a vowel at or before it. pf: fs, and the word comes right before
; a pause. bef: a vowel came earlier in this word, as the segment found it.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            rec     INP   kind     03-17: a segment; a pause is 0 0 0
  04                    INP   s
  05                    INP   wf
  06                    INP   after
  07                    INP   imm
  08                    INP   nvs
  09                    INP   pfw
  10                    CLA   kind
  11                    SUB   c8
  12                    TAC   sound
  13                    CLA   z
  14                    STO   s
  15                    STO   fs
  16                    STO   pf
  17                    JMP   out
  18            sound   CLA   wf       18-45: bef, and a consonant's stress
  19                    SUB   00
  20                    TAC   kw
  21                    CLA   z
  22                    STO   bef
  23            kw      CLA   kind
  24                    SUB   n2
  25                    TAC   vow
  26                    CLA   imm
  27                    SUB   00
  28                    TAC   ci
  29                    JMP   one
  30            ci      CLA   bef
  31                    SUB   00
  32                    TAC   cn
  33                    JMP   zero
  34            cn      CLA   nvs
  35                    SUB   00
  36                    TAC   zero
  37            one     CLA   00
  38                    JMP   sst
  39            zero    CLA   z
  40            sst     STO   s
  41                    CLA   z
  42                    STO   syl
  43                    JMP   fsx
  44            vow     CLA   00
  45                    STO   syl
  46            fsx     CLA   z        46-65: fs = no vowel after, and a vowel here or before; pf = pfw and fs
  47                    STO   fs
  48                    CLA   after
  49                    SUB   00
  50                    TAC   na
  51                    JMP   pfx
  52            na      CLA   syl
  53                    ADD   bef
  54                    SUB   00
  55                    TAC   pfx
  56                    CLA   00
  57                    STO   fs
  58            pfx     CLA   pfw
  59                    ADD   fs
  60                    SUB   n2
  61                    TAC   p0
  62                    CLA   00
  63                    JMP   pfs
  64            p0      CLA   z
  65            pfs     STO   pf
  66            out     OUT   s        66-76: the four cards; after a vowel, a vowel came before
  67                    OUT   fs
  68                    OUT   pf
  69                    OUT   bef
  70                    CLA   kind
  71                    SUB   n2
  72                    TAC   setb
  73                    JMP   rec
  74            setb    CLA   00
  75                    STO   bef
  76                    JMP   rec
  80            kind    DATA  0
  81            s       DATA  0
  82            wf      DATA  0
  83            after   DATA  0
  84            imm     DATA  0
  85            nvs     DATA  0
  86            pfw     DATA  0
  87            fs      DATA  0
  88            pf      DATA  0
  89            bef     DATA  0
  90            syl     DATA  0
  91            z       DATA  0
  92            c8      DATA  8
  93            n2      DATA  2
